Sotto service-worker content-cache recheck (Gate 1 follow-up)
Date: 2026-09-05
Repo: /Users/noelturlington/Claude/sotto (read-only session; this log is the only file written)

===========================================================================
1. WHAT WAS CHECKED
===========================================================================
Gate 1 previously found that after opening a book and playing its
narration in the static-exported PWA build, the service worker's content
cache held only "1 file for this book" when it should hold both the
chapter JSON and the narration mp3. This session re-read apps/client/public/sw.js
in full, rebuilt the static export, served it locally, drove a real
Chromium (Playwright) through open-book + play-narration, and inspected
Cache Storage directly.

===========================================================================
2. sw.js CACHING LOGIC (read in full; file is 135 lines)
===========================================================================
Cache names (sw.js:19-21):
  SHELL_CACHE_PREFIX   = 'sotto-shell-'    -> sotto-shell-<manifest.version>
  CONTENT_CACHE_PREFIX = 'sotto-content-'  -> sotto-content-<manifest.version>

fetch handler (sw.js:93-135):
  - sw.js:94-96: any cross-origin request, or non-GET, is left alone
    (`if (url.origin !== self.location.origin) return;`) -- the worker
    never calls respondWith for it, so it can NEVER end up in either cache.
  - sw.js:98-105: `/content/packs` or `/content/packs/index.json` ->
    networkFirst() into the content cache.
  - sw.js:107-114: everything else under `/content/packs/` ->
    cacheFirst() into the content cache. THIS BRANCH HAS NO FILE-TYPE
    FILTER: it matches on url.pathname.startsWith('/content/packs/') only.
    There is no check on extension (.json vs .mp3), no size limit, no
    check of response.headers/content-type, and no special-casing of
    Range requests. cacheFirst() (sw.js:71-78) does `if (response.ok)
    await cache.put(...)` for whatever comes back, regardless of type.
  - sw.js:119-134: everything else (app shell) -> cacheFirst into the
    shell cache, with an offline navigate-fallback to cached index.html.

CONCLUSION FROM READING THE CODE: sw.js itself does not discriminate
between the chapter JSON and the narration mp3. Both are handled by the
exact same cacheFirst() code path under the exact same cache name. Any
"only 1 file cached" symptom is NOT caused by an extension/path filter in
sw.js.

