===========================================================================
4. FIRST ATTEMPT: plain http://localhost:8092 -- ALL content caching bypassed
===========================================================================
Drove the Browser-pane Chromium instance to http://localhost:8092/reader/es-fabulas-samaniego,
then (after that stalled on unrelated tool issues) confirmed via a
Playwright script against the same URL:

  [request] GET http://localhost:8790/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/book.json
  [request] GET http://localhost:8790/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/audio/01.mp3
  [request] GET http://localhost:8790/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/chapters/01.json

Every /content/packs/** request went to a DIFFERENT ORIGIN
(http://localhost:8790, the apps/server dev port) than the page itself
(http://localhost:8092). Root cause, read directly:

  apps/client/src/state/contentApi.ts:27-35
    export function serverUrl(): string {
      const configured = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL;
      if (configured) return configured;
      const loc = (globalThis as { location?: { hostname: string; origin: string } }).location;
      if (loc && !/^(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\])$/.test(loc.hostname)) return loc.origin;
      return 'http://localhost:8790';
    }

  When the export is served at a bare hostname of exactly "localhost" (as
  instructed: port 8092 on localhost), loc.hostname === 'localhost' matches
  the regex, so the same-origin branch is skipped and the function falls
  through to the hardcoded dev-server fallback 'http://localhost:8790'.
  Combined with sw.js:95 (`if (url.origin !== self.location.origin) return;`),
  every single content request becomes cross-origin and the service worker
  never touches it at all -- NEITHER the JSON NOR the mp3 is cached. Cache
  Storage after this run contained only the sotto-shell-* cache; no
  sotto-content-* cache existed at all.

  This reproduces a *worse* symptom than Gate 1's "1 file cached" (here:
  0 files cached) and is a local-testing artifact of using the literal
  hostname "localhost", not the bug Gate 1 was describing. (The real
  deployment at sotto-steel.vercel.app has loc.hostname = 'sotto-steel.vercel.app',
  which does NOT match the regex, so it takes the same-origin branch and
  is not affected.)

  Worked around it the same way a prior session apparently did (evidence:
  network logs from an earlier browser-pane tab in this same session showed
  requests to http://sotto.localhost:8090/... instead of plain localhost) --
  "sotto.localhost" still resolves to loopback (RFC 6761 .localhost TLD)
  but does NOT match contentApi.ts's `^(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\])$`
  regex, so loc.origin is used and requests stay same-origin, exercising
  the real caching path.

===========================================================================
5. SECOND ATTEMPT: http://sotto.localhost:8092 -- same-origin, SW-controlled
===========================================================================
Script: Playwright/Chromium, es-419 locale book, real click on the Play
button (a genuine user-gesture click, not autoplay, since Chromium's
autoplay policy blocks unmuted playback without one -- confirmed by an
earlier pageerror: "play() failed because the user didn't interact with
the document first").

Sequence:
  1. First navigation to /reader/es-fabulas-samaniego (installs the SW).
     Requests during THIS load (book.json, chapters/01.json, audio/01.mp3,
     all 200 OK) are NOT SW-controlled -- this is standard, spec-mandated
     browser behavior: a page is never controlled by the service worker
     that it itself causes to install on that same navigation; control
     only takes effect on the next navigation (or immediately with
     clients.claim(), which sw.js:66 does call on 'activate', but that is
     still after this first load's requests have already gone out
     uncontrolled).
  2. Confirmed SW state: {"ok":true,"scope":"http://sotto.localhost:8092/","active":"activated"}
  3. page.reload() -- this second navigation IS SW-controlled.
     Requests fired on reload: only audio/01.mp3 (chapters/01.json was
     NOT re-requested -- the chapter text was already in the app's
     persisted/in-memory store from step 1 and simply wasn't fetched
     again over the network).
  4. Clicked the real "Play"/"Lecture" button (aria-label "Lecture" --
     UI locale rendered as French in this profile) and let narration run
     6s.

Final Cache Storage dump (full key listing):

  sotto-shell-1788580818173.4204 (64 entries -- app shell: entry JS,
  fonts, icons, index.html, manifest.webmanifest, etc. -- omitted here
  for brevity, see raw run log)

  sotto-content-1788580818173.4204 (3 entries):
    http://sotto.localhost:8092/content/packs
    http://sotto.localhost:8092/content/packs/fr-FR/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/audio/01.mp3
    http://sotto.localhost:8092/content/packs/es-419/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/audio/01.mp3

VERDICT: hasJson = false, hasMp3 = true.
  -> Exactly the MIRROR IMAGE of Gate 1's report (they saw JSON cached,
     audio not; this run shows audio cached, JSON not). Same underlying
     mechanism, opposite direction, confirming the mechanism is
     "whichever resource was actually re-fetched over the network while
     the SW was in control", not a type-based filter in sw.js.

  Root cause of the asymmetry: chapters/01.json is fetched once, on the
  first (uncontrolled) load, and then served from the app's own
  client-side store on every subsequent view of that chapter -- so it is
  never re-issued as a network GET while the SW is active, and therefore
  never has a chance to land in Cache Storage even though sw.js would
  gladly cache it if asked. The narration mp3, by contrast, is
  re-fetched by expo-audio's createAudioPlayer({ uri }) (apps/client/src/platform/audio.ts:40,
  called from useNarrationPlayer) every time the player is
  (re)constructed -- e.g. on every reload/remount -- so it keeps getting
  a fresh network request that the now-active SW intercepts and caches.
  Under Gate 1's original sequence of interactions the same mechanism
  produced the opposite outcome (JSON got a fresh SW-controlled fetch,
  audio did not).

  Practical implication: a book opened for the FIRST time ever in a
  session (single navigation, no reload) will cache NOTHING under
  sotto-content-* for that book, by design/spec (first load is
  uncontrolled). "Offline after opening once" only actually holds once a
  second navigation (reload, or navigating away and back via a full
  reload) happens while the SW is active, and even then, only the
  specific sub-resources that get re-requested over the network end up
  cached -- resources served from client-side app state on repeat views
  do not.

===========================================================================
6. SECONDARY BUG NOTICED (tangential, not the JSON/mp3 question)
===========================================================================
On reload, the app requested
  http://sotto.localhost:8092/content/packs/fr-FR/books/es-fabulas-samaniego/audio/01.mp3
-- fr-FR does not contain a book called "es-fabulas-samaniego" (only
es-419 does; confirmed via `find dist/content/packs/fr-FR -iname
'*samaniego*'` returning nothing). serve-static.mjs's SPA-fallback
(serve-static.mjs:56-60) answers any non-existent path with dist/index.html
(text/html, 200 OK) rather than a 404, so the SW's cacheFirst() (response.ok
is true for a 200) happily cached that bogus HTML body under the real
.mp3 URL key -- see the fr-FR entry in the cache dump above. This looks
like a separate client-side locale bug (something requesting the mp3
under the UI locale, fr-FR, instead of the book's actual contentLocale,
es-419) worth its own look, but is unrelated to the sw.js JSON-vs-mp3
question this task was scoped to.

